%% title: Standing Order Creation and Execution Flow
sequenceDiagram
    participant CLIENT as Client (admin-ui / customer app)
    participant SVC as StandingOrderService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant OB as OutboxDispatcher
    participant K as Kafka
    participant TXN as transaction-service (consumer)

    note over CLIENT: Create standing order
    CLIENT->>SVC: POST /api/v1/standing-orders
    SVC->>DB: findByIdempotencyKey → return if exists
    SVC->>DB: INSERT standing_orders (status=ACTIVE, next_execution_date=start_date)
    SVC->>DB: INSERT standing_order_outbox (StandingOrderCreated)
    SVC-->>CLIENT: 201 Created

    note over OB: Outbox dispatch (every 5s)
    OB->>DB: listProcessable
    OB->>K: publish openbank.standing-orders.order.event (StandingOrderCreated)
    OB->>DB: markSent

    K-->>TXN: StandingOrderCreated event consumed

    note over SVC: Execution scheduler (TBD — port defined, not yet wired)
    SVC->>DB: listDueForExecution(today) — standing_orders WHERE next_execution_date <= today AND status=ACTIVE
    loop per due order
        SVC->>K: publish StandingOrderExecuted (triggers payment in transaction-service)
        SVC->>DB: UPDATE standing_orders next_execution_date, last_execution_date, execution_count++
    end

    note over CLIENT: Lifecycle management
    CLIENT->>SVC: POST /api/v1/standing-orders/{id}/pause
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE standing_orders status=PAUSED
    SVC->>DB: INSERT outbox (StandingOrderPaused)

    CLIENT->>SVC: POST /api/v1/standing-orders/{id}/resume
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE standing_orders status=ACTIVE
    SVC->>DB: INSERT outbox (StandingOrderResumed)

    CLIENT->>SVC: DELETE /api/v1/standing-orders/{id}
    SVC->>DB: UPDATE standing_orders status=CANCELLED
    SVC->>DB: INSERT outbox (StandingOrderCancelled)
    SVC->>K: publish StandingOrderCancelled
